<title>UK: NFC sells Lynx to MBO for 26 mln stg.</title>
<headline>NFC sells Lynx to MBO for 26 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British freight firm NFC Plc said it had sold its Lynx express parcels service to local management backed by National Westminster Bank's NatWest Ventures Ltd, for 26 million stg.</p>
<p>The price comprises 23 million stg in cash, with the balance due on certain contingencies, secured by preference shares.</p>
<p>Completion of the sale was announced earlier today as part of a wider rationalisation and sell-off of non-core businesses by NFC.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
